  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and that renames must go through deprecation. A hard rename would break them as soon as it deployed. So the event now publishes both names with identical values. The old fields are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`.\n\nI changed `src/core/events.ts` and `test/app.test.ts`. The tests now check the event has the new fields and that they match the old ones.\n\nI left the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the internal `Order` model on `totalCents` and `placedAt`. ARCH-8 requires that response to stay backward compatible, and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. After that, `totalCents` and `placedAt` can be dropped from the event, ideally with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4. I didn't bump the version now, since adding fields doesn't need it.",
